{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and motion capabilities, separating sensor outcomes from motion commands. The specification enforces safe, coverage-biased exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are used only when obstacles are detected. Recovery is directed by obstacle side, and full_rotate is reserved for rare, persistent blockage. All transitions are deterministic, and uncontrollable events are always handled first.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for sensing and motion to enable modular specification.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk in clear, short move_forward bursts, directed turn recovery, and rare full_rotate for persistent blockage."
  ],
